 Settings › Fonts and text

 Font
   font-name              unifont
   font-frits             /etc/vtium/fonts (default)
   font-paths             unset (default)
   font-engine            unset (default)
   font-ligatures         off (default)

 Font size and spacing
   font-size              0 (default)
   font-hinting           unset (default)
   font-line-spacing      unset (default)

 Box drawing and block characters
   glyph-source           unset (default)
   glyph-source-box       unset (default)

 Press Enter to type a setting's value, or to pick it from a list when the setting takes a fixed
 set of values. Leave a typed value empty to use the default.
 The console's font. The value is the name of a font set (a frit file, `NAME.vtfrit` in
 `/etc/vtium/fonts`). It can also be the name of a kbd console font, or the absolute path of a font
 file, such as a PSF, BDF or TrueType font; vtium then uses that one font. When unset, vtium uses
 the font from vconsole.conf, or else the font set `terminus`. If vtium cannot find the font, it …

